   "metadata": {
    "id": "JxxFVrR5wU8b"
   },
   "source": [
    "**Analyze and Conclusion**: We used Kendall's Tau Correlation Test to see if there was a relationship between ethical concerns and verify likelihood because there are two categorical (ordinal) variables, and we are pulling data from a small dataset. Our tau correlation coefficient of about 0.28 shows a weak positive correlation between ethical concerns and verify likelihood, meaning that those who are more concerned with the ethical usage of AI are more likely to verify if content on their social media feed is AI-generated. Our p-value of less than 0.05 shows that the relationship is statistically signficiant and is unlikely due to random chance.\n",
    "\n"
   ]
